  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.4.2\n      - Docs: complete XML documentation across the entire public API surface; missing-doc\n        and malformed-cref warnings are now promoted to build errors so the doc surface\n        can never silently regress.\n      - Fix: the screenshot index.md now lists every viewport actually captured (was\n        hardcoded to desktop + mobile) and no longer links cells for screenshots that\n        weren't taken.\n\n      0.4.1\n      - Fix: scroll-reveal content now captured. IntersectionObserver is neutralized in the\n        browser context so elements that start hidden (opacity:0) and reveal on scroll are\n        rendered in headless full-page screenshots instead of staying invisible.\n      - Fix: first-run TestServer race. Fixture startup retries the intermittent\n        \"server has not been started\" error from the dual-host pattern (common on cold CI),\n        so consumers no longer need pipeline retries.\n\n      0.4.0\n      - New: opt-in AllowedExternalHosts on both fixture bases. Permits specific external\n        hosts (e.g. font/icon CDNs) through hermetic routing so captures render faithfully;\n        default stays empty (fully hermetic). Allowing live hosts reintroduces a network\n        dependency, so prefer self-hosting and keep the list small.\n\n      0.3.0\n      - New: ScreenshotFixtureBaseNoDb<TFactory> for consumers without EF Core.\n      - New: ViewportSpec record; presets Desktop/Mobile/Tablet/Wide; consumers can declare custom sizes inline.\n      - Change: graduates off the 0.x-alpha track.\n      - Breaking: BrowserContextHelpers.NewAnonContextAsync / NewAuthedContextAsync now take ViewportSpec instead of string.\n      - Breaking: ScreenshotTestsBase.GetCases signature changed to GetCases(routes, viewports).\n      - Breaking: IScreenshotFixture context methods take ViewportSpec.\n      - AuthedUserId is now virtual with default String.Empty (was abstract).",
